neighborhood ideal of a graph ... We show that if $G$ is a forest, then the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of $R/NI(G)$ is the same as the matching number of $G$, thus proving a conjecture of Sharifan and Moradi in the affirmative.\nThe main aim of this paper is to show that several classes of graphs, including outerplanar graphs and threshold graphs, satisfy this conjecture. We do this by studying various graph operations and examining how they affect the number of zero forcing sets.\n\ngraph outerplanar coloring\n\n2024-01-09 v4\n\nShiny Chakraborty, Ajay P. Joseph, Amit Roy, Anurag Singh\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nCastelnuovo-Mumford regularity of the closed neighborhood ideal of a graph\n\nPublished in Journal of Algebraic Combinatorics, 61(1), 2025 • View Publication • BIB\n\nLet $G$ be a finite simple graph and let $NI(G)$ denote the closed neighborhood ideal of $G$ in a polynomial ring $R$. We show that if $G$ is a forest, then the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of $R/NI(G)$ is the same as the matching number of $G$, thus proving a conjecture of Sharifan and Moradi in the affirmative. We also show that the matching number of $G$ provides a lower bound for the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of $R/NI(G)$ for any $G$. Furthermore, we prove that, if $G$ contains a simplicial vertex, then $NI(G)$ admits a Betti splitting, and consequently, we show that the projective dimension of $R/NI(G)$ is also bounded below by the matching number of $G$, if $G$ is a forest or a unicyclic graph.\n\ncastelnuovo-mumford contain graph polynomial ring simple graph matching polynomial\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAnurag Singh - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/author/anurag-singh)\nciteturn3search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of the closed neighborhood ideal of a graph ... We show that if $G$ is a forest, then the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of $R/NI